div data-track-click-shared=\"{&quot;product_field&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;element_name&quot;:&quot;author_bio&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:&quot;navigation&quot;}\" data-track-view=\"{&quot;subscription_experience&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;product_field&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;element_name&quot;:&quot;author_bio&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:&quot;module_in_view&quot;}\" data-load-strategy=\"exclude\" data-component-type=\"post-bottom-authors\">\n            <div>\n                <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/author/lloyd-lee\" data-track-click=\"{&quot;index&quot;:1}\">\n                      <div data-slug=\"lloyd-lee\">\n                          <p><img data-old-src=\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 1 1'%3E%3C/svg%3E\" src=\"https://i.insider.com/655528f322cf74a5739809f5?crop=1:1&width=256&format=jpeg&auto=webp\" alt=\"Lloyd Lee\">\n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        </p>  </div>\n                </a>\n        \n              <p><a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/author/lloyd-lee\" data-track-click=\"{&quot;index&quot;:1}\">Lloyd Lee</a>\n        \n                \n          <span data-disable-for-sooth-user=\"\" data-component-type=\"follow-button\" data-load-strategy=\"lazy\" role=\"tooltip\" data-tooltip-position=\"middle\" data-tooltip-active=\"false\" data-state=\"\" data-topic-type=\"author\" data-topic-slug=\"lloyd-lee\" data-topic-link=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/author/lloyd-lee\" data-topic-label=\"Lloyd Lee\" data-topic-location=\"author_bio\" data-topic-shortened-label=\"Lloyd\" data-topic-image=\"{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;655528f322cf74a5739809f5&quot;,&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Lloyd Lee&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:4566,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;Insider&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:3043},&quot;links&quot;:{&quot;self&quot;:&quot;https://i.insider.com/655528f322cf74a5739809f5&quot;}}\">\n            \n          \n            <div>\n              <p>\n                  You're currently following this author!\n           Click to unsubscribe from email alerts.\n              </p>\n            </div>\n            \n          </span>\n            </p></div>\n        \n            <div>\n              <p><span>Lloyd Lee is a reporter at Business Insider covering frontier technologies, with a focus on how they're being deployed in the real world and the gaps and tensions that emerge as people, companies, and regulators respond. His coverage has featured&#160;<a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/waymo-robotaxi-lidar-sensor-versus-cameras-vision-only-2025-5\">autonomous vehicles</a>, <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/rivian-layoffs-r2-production-rj-scaringe-critical-moment-2025-10\">EVs</a>, <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/robot-dogs-quadruped-data-center-security-boston-dynamics-ghost-robotics-2026-3\">robotics</a>, <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/paradromics-first-long-term-brain-chip-patient-neurosurgeon-engineer-2026-6\">brain-computer interfaces</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/microsoft-ai-ceo-mustafa-suleyman-white-collar-tasks-automation-prediction-2026-2\">AI</a>.</span><span>Lloyd's reporting on the progress of <a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/tesla-vs-waymo-full-self-driving-fsd-robotaxi-lidar-cameras-2025-5\">Alphabet's Waymo and Tesla's autonomous ambitions</a> was recognized by the San Francisco Press Club with a Bay Area Journalism Award.Before joining Business Insider, he was a local reporter for Almanac News and Palo Alto Weekly, covering housing issues, small businesses, and notable Silicon Valley characters.</span><span>Lloyd is based in San Francisco.He can be reached via email lloydlee@businessinsider.com, or by phone at 646-768-1630, or Signal at lloyd.71.</span>\n              </p>\n              </div>\n          </div>\n    \n          \n          \n          \n          <div data-component-type=\"post-category-tags\" data-load-strategy=\"lazy\" data-track-marfeel=\"post-category-tags\">\n            <ul data-track-click-shared=\"{&quot;product_field&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:&quot;navigation&quot;,&quot;element_name&quot;:&quot;category_link&quot;}\">\n                \n                <li>\n                  <a data-track-click=\"\" href=\"/category/tesla\" title=\"Tesla\">Tesla</a>\n                </li>\n          \n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n    \n    \n          <section data-track-page-area=\"Post Bottom\">\n          <!-- Included desktop \"taboola\" -->    <vendor-taboola data-component-type=\"vendor-taboola\" data-root-margin=\"0px 0px 100% 0px\" data-consent=\"MARKETING\" config=\"{&quot;providerName&quot;:&quot;taboola&quot;,&quot;providerPageType&quot;:{&quot;article&quot;:&quot;auto&quot;},&quot;providerUrl&quot;:&quot;https://cdn.taboola.com/libtrc/businessinsider/loader.js&quot;,&quot;providerPrivacyLoader&quot;:&quot;https://static.tblcontent.com/libtrc/businessinsider/loader.privacy.js&quot;,&quot;providerPixel&quot;:&quot;https://static.qovani.com/libtrc/tr5?type=pixel&publisher=businessinsider&quot;,&quot;providerFlushValue&quot;:{&quot;flush&quot;:true},&quot;providerData&quot;:{&quot;mode&quot;:&quot;thumbs-1r&quot;,&quot;container&quot;:&quot;taboola-below-main-column&quot;,&quot;placement&quot;:&quot;Below Article Thumbnails Logged Out&quot;,&quot;target_type&quot;:&quot;mix&quot;}}\" data-load-strategy=\"defer\">\n                \n              </vendor-taboola>\n          \n          <!-- Excluded mobile \"taboola\" --></section>\n    \n      </section>\n  </section>\n\n  \n  \n\n\n    <back-to-home data-component-type=\"back-to-home\" data-load-strategy=\"defer\" data-only-on=\"mobile\" inert=\"\">\n      \n  \n      \n  \n      \n    </back-to-home>\n</section></DIV>","content_text":"By Lloyd Lee You're currently following this author! Click to unsubscribe from email alerts. Harald Tittel/picture alliance via Getty Images Tesla Robotaxi uses a fleet of Model Ys, but the terms of service limit seating to 4 people. 2026-11-19T02:29:00.049Z Elon Musk said Tesla plans to develop a steering-wheel-free, pedal-free version of the Model Y capable of carrying six or seven passengers, though he didn't explain how the company would configure the vehicle's interior.The Tesla CEO said on Wednesday at The New York Times DealBook Summit that the Cybercab — a two-seater coupe with no steering wheel or pedals — will cover most of the passenger miles driven for the company's robotaxi service, but the need for a bigger autonomous car is still there.\"If you've got a whole family in the car, you still need autonomous vehicles for that, so what we plan to do is have an autonomous version of Model Y that wouldn't have steering wheels and pedals and would be good for transporting groups of six or seven people,\" Musk said.Tesla Robotaxi already uses Model Ys in its autonomous vehicle fleet, but it can transport only up to four passengers.A robotaxi capable of carrying six or seven passengers would give Tesla a way to serve larger groups, a segment of the US autonomous ride-hailing market that remains relatively underserved.Waymo's Ojai, which is supposed to be the company's more spacious vehicle platform compared to the Jaguar SUVs, can fit up to four people.Uber plans to launch robotaxis with Lucid's Gravity SUV, which the ride-hailing company said can seat six people. Read next Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Business Insider tells the innovative stories you want to know Lloyd Lee You're currently following this author! Click to unsubscribe from email alerts. Lloyd Lee is a reporter at Business Insider covering frontier technologies, with a focus on how they're being deployed in the real world and the gaps and tensions that emerge as people, companies, and regulators respond. His coverage has featured autonomous vehicles, EVs, robotics, brain-computer interfaces, and AI.Lloyd's reporting on the progress of Alphabet's Waymo and Tesla's autonomous ambitions was recognized by the San Francisco Press Club with a Bay Area Journalism Award.Before joining Business Insider, he was a local reporter for Almanac News and Palo Alto Weekly, covering housing issues, small businesses, and notable Silicon Valley characters.Lloyd is based in San Francisco.He can be reached via email lloydlee@businessinsider.com, or by phone at 646-768-1630, or Signal at lloyd.71. Tesla","fetched_at":"2026-11-20T06:19:40.318Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<p><span>By</span>\n                                  \n                                  \n                                  \n                                    <span data-e2e-name=\"Lloyd Lee\">\n                                  \n                                      <span>\n                                        <a data-e2e-name=\"byline-author-name\" href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/author/lloyd-lee\">Lloyd Lee</a>        \n                                    <span data-disable-for-sooth-user=\"\" data-component-type=\"follow-button\" data-load-strategy=\"lazy\" role=\"tooltip\" data-tooltip-position=\"middle\" data-tooltip-active=\"false\" data-state=\"\" data-topic-type=\"author\" data-topic-slug=\"lloyd-lee\" data-topic-link=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/author/lloyd-lee\" data-topic-label=\"Lloyd Lee\" data-topic-location=\"byline\" data-topic-shortened-label=\"Lloyd\" data-topic-image=\"{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;655528f322cf74a5739809f5&quot;,&quot;attributes&quot;:{&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Lloyd 